# V-6 — M0-T5 **PASS** (V-1 is closed) · one confirmed defect, 2 cells, R0-blocking

All four deliverables verified. **V-1 is closed.** Nine angles; eight pass, the ninth found two
false cells with a root cause that is **not the builder's fault** and that deserves its own
Defect Register entry.

## What I verified rather than read

| Deliverable | Result |
|---|---|
| **A** Efficiency sheet | 10 → **11 sheets**; 128 rows; all nine §16 columns present |
| **B** five absent §15 fields | 0 → **128** each (bound class, hotspot, technique, identity proof, speedup, rows/sec, target, p50/p90/profiled) |
| **C1** hotspot false green | `no bespoke speed work` **64 → 0**; hotspot **null on 128/128** |
| **C2** timeout-source constant | **107 registered / 21 default** — matches the live distribution I measured myself in V-2, exactly |

**D-8's per-template precision held in both directions.** The two carve-outs survive: `Not a
build; nothing to speed up` **8 → 8 kept**, `Built once, reused by every chart` **40 → 40 kept**.

**You asked me to hunt for a legitimate classification destroyed by an over-broad sweep. There
isn't one, and I measured it rather than eyeballing it.** Of the 64 swept assets: **0** had their
measured `Now:` line changed, **0** lack the new ledger line, **0** have a null p50, and **0**
blocks shrank. Across all 128, **not one block is shorter than its pre-T5 version.** The sweep
added information and destroyed none.

Also verified: the plan is **byte-identical outside the markers** (against the true pre-T5
baseline `29cfdfbc2`), and the workbook and markdown **agree on all 128** timeout-source values —
the single-source property is intact.

**`rows/sec = null` on 128/128 — challenge withdrawn on the evidence.** The builder invited this
as its uncertainty #1, so I checked the premise instead of deferring: `information_schema` for
`build_run_assets` returns exactly `run_id, asset_id, position, state, started_at, ended_at,
error`. **No row-count column, no chart_id.** The value genuinely is not derivable. The refusal to
print it is the doctrine, correctly applied.

